.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_chan
provides typed channel primitives for cross-task / cross-process /
cross-thread message passing.  Each channel kind has different
fan-in / fan-out semantics:
.Bl -tag -width "broadcast" -offset indent
.It oneshot
A single message; one sender, one receiver.  Used for request /
reply patterns, one-shot futures.
.Fn xtc_chan_oneshot_create
and
.Fn xtc_chan_oneshot_destroy
manage the channel;
.Fn xtc_chan_oneshot_send
delivers the single message;
.Fn xtc_chan_oneshot_try_recv
polls for it; and
.Fn xtc_chan_oneshot_set_waker
registers an
.Vt xtc_waker_t
for async readiness notification.
.It mpsc
Multiple producers, single consumer.  Bounded ring buffer.  Lock-
free producer side using sequence-number CAS; consumer needs no
synchronisation.
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_create
takes a
.Va capacity ;
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_try_send
and
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_try_recv
move messages without parking;
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_set_waker
arms an async waker;
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_close
marks the channel closed; and
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_len
reports the queued count.
.Fn xtc_chan_mpsc_destroy
frees it.
.It mpmc
Multiple producers, multiple consumers.  Bounded ring buffer
serialising both sides via per-slot sequence numbers
.Pq Vyukov-style queue .
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_create ,
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_try_send ,
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_try_recv ,
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_close ,
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_len ,
and
.Fn xtc_chan_mpmc_destroy
mirror the MPSC entry points.
.It watch
Single-producer, multi-consumer of latest-value-only state.
Useful for config that may change while readers want the current
view.
.Fn xtc_chan_watch_create
and
.Fn xtc_chan_watch_destroy
manage the channel;
.Fn xtc_chan_watch_send
publishes a new latest value; and
.Fn xtc_chan_watch_recv
reads the current value.
.It broadcast
Multi-producer, multi-consumer fan-out.  Each subscribed
consumer sees every message.  Per-consumer lag tracking; slow
consumers see their queue fill and may drop.
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_create
and
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_destroy
manage the channel;
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_send
fans a message out;
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_subscribe
and
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_unsubscribe
add and remove a consumer cursor; and
.Fn xtc_chan_broadcast_recv
reads the next message for a subscriber, reporting a
.Va lagged
count of messages skipped when it fell behind.
.It demand
Pull-based, the reactive-streams / GenStage backpressure primitive.  The
consumer explicitly ASKS for
.Fa n
items with
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_ask ;
the producer's
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_send
succeeds only while there is outstanding demand (returning
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
when demand is exhausted or the buffer is full), so a fast producer
cannot outrun a slow consumer -- backpressure is expressed as demand,
not as a fixed buffer that drops or blocks.  Delivered items still
buffer up to
.Fa capacity ,
and the consumer drains them with
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_try_recv ,
which does NOT itself grant demand -- the consumer sets its own
high-water policy by calling
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_ask .
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_outstanding
and
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_len
report the un-consumed demand and the buffered item count.
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_set_producer_waker
fires when the consumer grants demand;
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_set_consumer_waker
fires when the producer sends an item;
.Fn xtc_chan_demand_close
closes the channel (buffered items still drain).
.El
.Pp
All channels are heap-allocated and reference-managed via the
optional
.Vt xtc_res_t
accountant; passing one charges memory against the cap.
.Pp
.Sy Ownership :
the sender transfers ownership of the message buffer to the
receiver.  After
.Fn xtc_chan_*_send
returns
.Dv XTC_OK ,
the sender must not free or further mutate the buffer.  The
receiver is responsible for freeing.
.Sh INTEGRATION WITH xtc_proc
For BEAM-style mailboxes use
.Xr xtc_proc 3
directly: every process has its own mailbox without any explicit
channel allocation.  Channels are for fan-in / fan-out patterns
that don't fit the per-proc-mailbox model:
.Bl -bullet -compact -offset indent
.It
A pool of N workers consuming from one MPSC queue.
.It
N producers feeding M consumers via MPMC.
.It
Config-change broadcasts via watch channels.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
MPSC work queue:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_chan_mpsc_t *q;
xtc_chan_mpsc_create(NULL, /* cap */ 1024, &q);

/* producer */
xtc_chan_mpsc_try_send(q, work_item);

/* consumer */
void *item;
if (xtc_chan_mpsc_try_recv(q, &item) == XTC_OK) {
    handle(item);
    free(item);
}
.Ed
